{"id":"longest-repeating-replacement","title":"Longest repeating character replacement","difficulty":"medium","pattern":"sliding window","statement":"<p>You may change at most <code>k</code> characters of the upper-case string <code>s</code>. Return the length of the longest substring of one repeated letter you can obtain.</p>","entry":{"python":"character_replacement","cpp":{"name":"characterReplacement","ret":"int","params":[["string","s"],["int","k"]]}},"kind":"function","compare":"exact","time_limit_ms":2000,"hints":["A window is fixable if its length minus its most frequent letter's count is at most k.","The max count never needs to decrease for the answer to stay correct: the window only grows when a better max appears."],"complexity":"O(n) time","starter":{"python":"def character_replacement(s, k):\n    pass\n","cpp":"int characterReplacement(string s, int k) {\n    \n}\n"},"tests":[{"args":["ABAB",2],"expected":4,"sample":true},{"args":["AABABBA",1],"expected":4,"sample":true},{"args":["A",0],"expected":1},{"args":["ABCDE",1],"expected":2},{"args":["AAAA",2],"expected":4},{"args":["",50],"expected":114}],"solution":{"explanation":"<p>Slide a window; it's valid if length \u2212 maxCount \u2264 k. When invalid, move the left edge one step (the window never shrinks below the best size). Keeping a stale maxCount is safe: the answer can only grow when maxCount grows. O(n \u00b7 26) or O(n).</p>","python":"import collections\n\ndef character_replacement(s, k):\n    cnt = collections.Counter(); left = best = maxf = 0\n    for right, c in enumerate(s):\n        cnt[c] += 1; maxf = max(maxf, cnt[c])\n        if right - left + 1 - maxf > k:\n            cnt[s[left]] -= 1; left += 1\n        best = max(best, right - left + 1)\n    return best\n","cpp":"int characterReplacement(string s, int k) {\n    int cnt[26] = {0}, left = 0, best = 0, maxf = 0;\n    for (int r = 0; r < (int)s.size(); r++) {\n        maxf = max(maxf, ++cnt[s[r] - 'A']);\n        if (r - left + 1 - maxf > k) cnt[s[left++] - 'A']--;\n        best = max(best, r - left + 1);\n    }\n    return best;\n}\n"}}